      Per-node macros used by ReplicatedMergeTree ZK paths and ON CLUSTER DDL.
      `{shard}` is `01` on both nodes (they're replicas of the same shard in
      cluster_1s2r). `{replica}` uniquely identifies the node.
      For exercise 42 (cluster_2s1r) we use literal shard numbers in DDL,
      not the macro — each node belongs to a different shard there.
    -->
